From: 77450danik <dnsystems@email.ua>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] comctl32: A toolbar not aligned to its parent keeps its width.

With CCS_NOPARENTALIGN and no CCS_NORESIZE, Windows sizes only the height of
a toolbar to its buttons; the place and the width stay what the program set.
Auto-sizing made it as wide as the parent: Rufus's row of four icons covered
its Start and Close buttons, and clicks on them went to the toolbar.
---
--- a/dll/win32/comctl32/toolbar.c
+++ b/dll/win32/comctl32/toolbar.c
@@ -3279,7 +3279,7 @@
 
         if (infoPtr->dwStyle & CCS_NOPARENTALIGN)
             uPosFlags |= SWP_NOMOVE;
-    
+
         if (!(infoPtr->dwStyle & CCS_NODIVIDER))
             cy += GetSystemMetrics(SM_CYEDGE);
 
@@ -3289,6 +3289,16 @@
             cy += 2 * GetSystemMetrics(SM_CYBORDER);
         }
 
+        /* Not aligned to the parent: only the height follows the buttons, the
+         * place and the width stay what the program gave (Rufus puts a short
+         * toolbar on the row of its Start button). The window's width already
+         * has its border. */
+        if (infoPtr->dwStyle & CCS_NOPARENTALIGN)
+        {
+            GetWindowRect(infoPtr->hwndSelf, &window_rect);
+            cx = window_rect.right - window_rect.left;
+        }
+
         SetWindowPos(infoPtr->hwndSelf, NULL, x, y, cx, cy, uPosFlags);
     }
 
